  iso:provenanceClause "9.3" ;
  iso:definition "Performance reporting addresses internal policies, procedures and processes, including risks, costs, value generated, asset health, life cycle performance, etc. The purpose of such reports is to recognize actual costs, to validate prior decisions, to recognize changes in value and to assess possible future value enhancements." ;
