  iso:definition "IFRS and US GAAP (or other GAAPs) require that the depreciation method used reflect the pattern in which the asset's future economic benefits are expected to be consumed by the organization. The organization should select the method that most closely reflects the expected pattern of consumption of the future economic benefits embodied in the asset and based on what is allowed from local jurisdictions." ;
